1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Translator's note

2
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:16,760
Do we go on where we left off yesterday,

3
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:20,200
or would you like to start something new?

4
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,840
Would you...

5
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:26,600
I thought there was a point that wasn't entirely clear

6
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:29,440
what we were discussing yesterday,

7
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:34,840
which is that we rather accepted that

8
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:38,360
security, psychological security, was wrong,

9
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:39,560
you know, was delusion.

10
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:42,520
But in general, I don't think we made it very clear

11
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:44,880
why it is a delusion.

12
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:48,560
You see, most people feel that psychological security

13
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:50,280
is a real thing and quite necessary,

14
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:52,680
and when it's disturbed, or when a person is frightened,

15
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:56,000
or sorrowful, or even so disturbed

16
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,040
that he might be psychologically disturbed

17
00:00:58,040 --> 00:00:59,400
and require treatment,

18
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:02,840
he feels that psychological security is necessary

19
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:05,720
before he can even begin to do anything.

20
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:06,720
That's right.

21
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:09,360
And I think that it isn't at all clear

22
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:12,880
why one should say that it's really not as important

23
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:15,120
as physical security.

24
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:18,680
Yes. No, I think we've made it fairly clear,

25
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:20,520
let's go into it.

26
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:21,520
Yes.

27
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:27,520
Is there really psychological security at all?

28
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:29,040
Well, I don't think we discussed

29
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:29,360
that fully.

30
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:29,380
Yes.

31
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:30,380
We discussed that fully last time.

32
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:33,380
Of course. Of course, nobody accepts that.

33
00:01:33,380 --> 00:01:35,380
But we are inquiring into it.

34
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:39,380
We are going into the problem of it.

35
00:01:39,380 --> 00:01:42,380
But we said something even deeper, I think, yesterday,

36
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:46,380
and that is that, at least as I was summarizing for myself,

37
00:01:46,380 --> 00:01:51,380
and that is that we felt, correct me if you think I'm wrong here,

38
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:59,340
that conditioning sets the stage

39
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:02,340
for the importance of psychological security,

40
00:02:02,340 --> 00:02:07,340
and that that in turn creates insecurity.

41
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:09,340
I mean, it's the conditioning that creates

42
00:02:09,340 --> 00:02:12,340
the psychological security as a focus.

43
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:13,340
Would you agree with that?

44
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:15,340
I think we two mean something different.

45
00:02:15,340 --> 00:02:21,340
Well, what do you mean?

46
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:25,340
First of all, sir, we take it for granted

47
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:28,340
that there is psychological security.

48
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:31,340
Okay. All right.

49
00:02:31,340 --> 00:02:33,340
Well, we think that we can get it.

50
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:35,340
We feel that there is.

51
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:38,340
Right. That's right.

52
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:40,340
Yes, I think that if you told somebody

53
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:42,340
who was feeling very disturbed mentally

54
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:44,340
that there is no psychological security,

55
00:02:44,340 --> 00:02:45,340
he would just feel a lot worse.

56
00:02:45,340 --> 00:02:48,340
Collapse. Of course.

57
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:50,340
Right. Right.

58
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:54,340
I mean, we are talking of fairly sane, rational people.

59
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,340
Okay.

60
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:59,300
We are questioning whether there is any reason

61
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:02,300
for any psychological security at all.

62
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:10,300
Permanency, stability, a sense of well-founded,

63
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:14,300
deep-rooted existence psychologically.

64
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:16,300
Maybe if we could say more then,

65
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:19,300
what would be psychological security?

66
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:21,300
I mean, after all, say, I believe.

67
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:24,300
I believe in something.

68
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:27,300
It may be the most foolish belief.

69
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:29,300
Right.

70
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:32,300
A neurotic belief. I believe in it.

71
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:34,300
Right.

72
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:38,300
And that gives you a tremendous sense of existence,

73
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:42,300
living and vitality and stability.

74
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:44,300
I think you could think of two examples.

75
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:46,300
One is if I could really believe that after dying

76
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:49,300
I would go to heaven and be quite sure of it,

77
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:50,300
then I could be very secure inwardly,

78
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:51,300
no matter what happened.

79
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:53,300
What? That would make you feel good.

80
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:55,300
Well, I'd say I don't really have to worry

81
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:57,300
because it's all a temporary trouble,

82
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:58,300
and I'm pretty sure that in time

83
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:00,300
it's all going to be very good, do you see?

84
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:03,300
That's the whole Asiatic attitude, more or less.

85
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:05,300
Or if I think I'm a communist,

86
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:08,300
I say in time communism is going to solve everything,

87
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:10,300
and we're going through a lot of troubles now,

88
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:12,300
but it's all going to be worthwhile and it'll work out,

89
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:14,300
and in the end it'll be all right.

90
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:15,300
Right.

91
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:16,300
If I could be sure of that,

92
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:18,300
then I'd say I feel very secure inside,

93
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:21,300
even if its conditions are hard.

94
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:23,300
Okay. All right.

95
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:26,300
So we are questioning,

96
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:28,300
though one has the strong belief

97
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:34,300
which gives them a sense of security, permanency,

98
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:39,300
whether there is such in reality, actuality...

99
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:41,300
You mean it's not possible.

100
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:44,300
The question is, is it possible?

101
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:46,300
Is it possible?

102
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:49,300
I may believe in God,

103
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:52,300
and that gives me a tremendous sense of...

104
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:54,300
Right.

105
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:57,300
...impermanency of this world,

106
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:58,300
but at least there is a sense

107
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:00,300
that there is permanency somewhere else.

108
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,300
Yeah, yeah.

109
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:03,300
But David, let me...

110
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:04,300
I want to ask David something.

111
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:06,300
Do you think that, for instance,

112
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:07,300
take a scientist,

113
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:09,300
a guy who's going to his laboratory every day,

114
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:11,300
or take a doctor.

115
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:15,300
He's getting security from going to...

116
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:17,300
I mean, he takes security

117
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:19,300
from the very routinization of his life.

118
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:20,300
From his knowledge.

119
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:22,300
Yes, from his knowledge.

120
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:24,300
If he keeps doing this,

121
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:25,300
he feels...

122
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:26,300
And the scientist,

123
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:27,300
where does he get security?

124
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:29,300
Well, he may believe he is learning

125
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:31,300
the permanent laws of nature,

126
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:33,300
you know, and really getting something

127
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:35,300
that means something.

128
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:36,300
Yeah.

129
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:38,300
And also getting a position in society

130
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:41,300
and being sure of his being well known

131
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:44,300
and respected and financially secure.

132
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,300
So he keeps...

133
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:46,300
He believes that these things

134
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:48,300
will give him the thing.

135
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:50,300
The mother believes that the child

136
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:52,300
will give her security, right?

137
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:56,300
So don't you psychologically have security?

138
00:05:56,300 --> 00:05:57,300
Yeah.

139
00:05:57,300 --> 00:05:58,300
Okay.

140
00:05:58,300 --> 00:05:59,300
Faith.

141
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:00,300
Right.

142
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:01,300
That's a good point.

143
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:03,300
I get a security out of my knowledge,

144
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:04,300
out of my routine,

145
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:06,300
out of my patience,

146
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:08,300
out of seeing my patients,

147
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:09,300
out of my position.

148
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:10,300
But there's conflict in that

149
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:12,300
because if I think it over a little bit,

150
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:13,300
I doubt it.

151
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:14,300
If I question it,

152
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:16,300
I say it doesn't look all that secure, right?

153
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:17,300
Anything may happen.

154
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:19,300
I mean, I say there may be a war,

155
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:20,300
there may be a depression,

156
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:21,300
there may be a flood.

157
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:22,300
Right.

158
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:23,300
There might be the same people

159
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:25,300
all of a sudden in the world.

160
00:06:26,300 --> 00:06:32,300
You think there's a chance.

161
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:34,300
So I say that then there's conflict

162
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:36,300
and confusion in my security

163
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:39,300
because I'm not sure about it.

164
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:40,300
You're not sure about it.

165
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:42,300
But if I had an absolute belief

166
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:44,300
in God and Heaven...

167
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:46,300
This is obvious.

168
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:47,300
It's obvious.

169
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:48,300
I agree with you.

170
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:49,300
It's obvious.

171
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:50,300
But I think it has to be...

172
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:51,300
In other words,

173
00:06:51,300 --> 00:06:53,300
it has to be really felt through.

174
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:55,300
But you, Dr. Schaefer...

175
00:06:55,300 --> 00:06:56,300
Right.

176
00:06:56,300 --> 00:06:57,300
You're the victim.

177
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:58,300
I'll be the victim.

178
00:06:58,300 --> 00:06:59,300
For the moment.

179
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:00,300
Okay.

180
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:02,300
Don't you have strong belief?

181
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:03,300
Right.

182
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:04,300
Well, I wouldn't say...

183
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:07,300
Don't you have a sense of permanency

184
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:09,300
somewhere inside you?

185
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,300
I think I do.

186
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,300
Psychologically?

187
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:12,300
Yeah, I do.

188
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:14,300
I mean, I have a sense of permanency

189
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:16,300
about my intention.

190
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:17,300
Intention?

191
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:19,300
I mean, you know, about my work,

192
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:22,300
my knowledge, my...

193
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:23,300
Status.

194
00:07:23,300 --> 00:07:24,300
My status,

195
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:26,300
the context,

196
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:28,300
the continuity of my interest.

197
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:29,300
Yeah.

198
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:30,300
You know what I mean?

199
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:31,300
Yes, yes.

200
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:33,300
In other words, that...

201
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:34,300
There's a sense of security

202
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:36,300
in the feeling that I can help someone.

203
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:37,300
Yes.

204
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:38,300
And I can do my work.

205
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:39,300
Okay?

206
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:40,300
Yes.

207
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:41,300
So, I mean, though...

208
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:42,300
That gives you security.

209
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:43,300
Psychologically.

210
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:44,300
Yeah, there's a certain something

211
00:07:44,300 --> 00:07:45,300
about it that's secure.

212
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:46,300
I don't feel...

213
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:47,300
What am I saying when I say security?

214
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:49,300
I'm saying that I won't be lonely.

215
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:50,300
No, no.

216
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:52,300
Feeling secure.

217
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:54,300
That you have something

218
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:55,300
that is imperishable.

219
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:57,300
Which means...

220
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:59,300
No, I don't feel it that way.

221
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:00,300
I feel it more in the sense of,

222
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:03,300
what is going to happen in time?

223
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:07,300
Am I going to have to depend on...

224
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:09,300
What is my time going to be?

225
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:10,300
Am I going to be lonely?

226
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:11,300
Is it going to be empty?

227
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:13,300
Isn't that security?

228
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:15,300
I mean, as Dr. Bohm pointed out,

229
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:18,300
if one has a strong belief

230
00:08:18,300 --> 00:08:20,300
in reincarnation,

231
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:23,300
as the whole Asiatic world has,

232
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:24,300
then...

233
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:26,300
Then it doesn't matter what happens.

234
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:29,300
Next life you have a better chance.

235
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:32,300
You might be miserable this life,

236
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:35,300
but next life you will be happier.

237
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:38,300
So that gives you a great sense of,

238
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:40,300
well, this is unimportant,

239
00:08:40,300 --> 00:08:41,300
but that is important.

240
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:43,300
Right, right.

241
00:08:43,300 --> 00:08:47,300
And that gives me a sense of great comfort,

242
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:49,300
great sense...

243
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:51,300
As though I was...

244
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:53,300
Well, this is a transient world anyhow.

245
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:54,300
Right.

246
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:56,300
And eventually I'll get there,

247
00:08:56,300 --> 00:08:57,300
something permanent.

248
00:08:57,300 --> 00:08:59,300
This is human...

249
00:08:59,300 --> 00:09:01,300
This is in the Asiatic world,

250
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:03,300
but I think in the Western world

251
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:04,300
you don't have that.

252
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:05,300
Oh, yes, you have it.

253
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:06,300
You have a different focus.

254
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:07,300
Of course.

255
00:09:07,300 --> 00:09:08,300
Well, it's different,

256
00:09:08,300 --> 00:09:09,300
but you always had the search for security.

257
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:10,300
I mean, either you...

258
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:11,300
Right, right.

259
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:13,300
But what do you think security is?

260
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:14,300
I mean, for instance,

261
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:16,300
you became a scientist,

262
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:17,300
you went to the laboratory,

263
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:21,300
you pick up the books all the time, right?

264
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:22,300
You never went to the laboratory,

265
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:23,300
but I mean, you had your own laboratory.

266
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:26,300
What the hell have you called security?

267
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:27,300
Security?

268
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:28,300
Yes.

269
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:30,300
I mean, what does he call his security?

270
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:31,300
His knowledge?

271
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:32,300
Having something.

272
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:36,300
No, having something to which you can cling to

273
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:38,300
and which is not perishable.

274
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:40,300
It may perish eventually,

275
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:45,300
but for the time being it is there to hold on.

276
00:09:45,300 --> 00:09:47,300
You can feel that it's permanent.

277
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:49,300
You see, like somebody in the past,

278
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:50,300
people used to accumulate gold

279
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:52,300
because gold is the symbol of the imperishable,

280
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,300
the heavenly.

281
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:54,300
I could feel that gold...

282
00:09:54,300 --> 00:09:56,300
We still have people who accumulate gold.

283
00:09:56,300 --> 00:09:57,300
We've got businessmen,

284
00:09:57,300 --> 00:09:58,300
they've got money.

285
00:09:58,300 --> 00:09:59,300
That gold really,

286
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:00,300
you feel it's really there.

287
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:01,300
It will never corrode,

288
00:10:01,300 --> 00:10:03,300
it will never vanish.

289
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:07,300
And you can count on it, you know.

290
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:10,300
So it's something that I can count on.

291
00:10:10,300 --> 00:10:13,300
Count on, hold on to, cling to,

292
00:10:13,300 --> 00:10:14,300
be attached to.

293
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:16,300
Believe in the me.

294
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:21,300
I know that I am a doctor.

295
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:23,300
I can depend on that.

296
00:10:23,300 --> 00:10:24,300
Knowledge.

297
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:25,300
Right, knowledge.

298
00:10:25,300 --> 00:10:26,300
Experience.

299
00:10:26,300 --> 00:10:27,300
Experience.

300
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:30,300
And the other hand, tradition.

301
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:31,300
Tradition.

302
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:33,300
I know that if I do this with a patient

303
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:34,300
that I'll get this result.

304
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,300
I might not get any good results,

305
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:37,300
but I'll get this result.

306
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:38,300
Yes.

307
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:40,300
So I think that's fairly clear.

308
00:10:40,300 --> 00:10:42,300
Yes, it's clear enough that we have that.

309
00:10:42,300 --> 00:10:45,300
You see, that's part of the society.

310
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:46,300
Part of our conditioning.

311
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:47,300
Part of our conditioning,

312
00:10:47,300 --> 00:10:52,300
that we want something secure and permanent.

313
00:10:52,300 --> 00:10:54,300
At least we think so.

314
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:55,300
We want immortality.

315
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:56,300
I think you see,

316
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:59,300
at Krishnaji's point about the Eastern world,

317
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:00,300
there is, I think,

318
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:03,300
a feeling in the West of wanting immortality.

319
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:05,300
Which is the same thing.

320
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:10,300
Well, wouldn't you say that insofar as thought can project time,

321
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:13,300
that it wants to be able to project everything all right in the future

322
00:11:13,300 --> 00:11:14,300
as far as possible.

323
00:11:14,300 --> 00:11:15,300
That's what I meant when I said loneliness.

324
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:17,300
If I don't have to have my loneliness.

325
00:11:17,300 --> 00:11:18,300
But you see, in other words,

326
00:11:18,300 --> 00:11:20,300
the anticipation of what is coming

327
00:11:20,300 --> 00:11:22,300
is already the present feeling.

328
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:25,300
See, if you can anticipate that something bad may come,

329
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:27,300
you already feel bad, right?

330
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:28,300
Does that seem clear?

331
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:29,300
That's right.

332
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:30,300
Therefore you would like to get rid of that.

333
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:32,300
So you'd like to anticipate that it won't happen.

334
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:34,300
That it will all be good.

335
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:35,300
Right.

336
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:37,300
I should say security would be the anticipation

337
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:39,300
that everything will be good in the future.

338
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:40,300
Good.

339
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:41,300
Continuous.

340
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:42,300
Or it will become better.

341
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:43,300
If it's not so good now,

342
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:46,300
it will become good with absolute certainty.

343
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:49,300
So then security is becoming.

344
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:51,300
Yes, becoming.

345
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:52,300
But...

346
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:53,300
Perfecting.

347
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:54,300
Right.

348
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:55,300
Becoming better.

349
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:56,300
I was thinking of what you were saying the other day

350
00:11:56,300 --> 00:11:57,300
about the Brahmin.

351
00:11:57,300 --> 00:12:00,300
Anybody can become a Brahmin,

352
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:02,300
then that gives him security.

353
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:03,300
Of course.

354
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:07,300
That is a projected belief,

355
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:10,300
a projected idea,

356
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:16,300
a comforting, satisfying concept.

357
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:17,300
Right.

358
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:18,300
You see, I see patients all the time.

359
00:12:18,300 --> 00:12:20,300
You know what their projected belief is?

360
00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:21,300
I will become...

361
00:12:21,300 --> 00:12:25,300
I will find somebody to love me.

362
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,300
I see patients who say,

363
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:29,300
I will become the chief of the department.

364
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:31,300
I will become the most famous doctor,

365
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:32,300
one man said.

366
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:33,300
I will become...

367
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:37,300
And his whole life goes like that.

368
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:39,300
Of course, it's also all focused on being

369
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:40,300
the best tennis player.

370
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:42,300
Of course, of course.

371
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:44,300
Well, I mean, it seems that it's all focused

372
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:47,300
on anticipating that life is going to be good.

373
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:48,300
Would you say that?

374
00:12:48,300 --> 00:12:50,300
Yes, life is going to be good.

375
00:12:50,300 --> 00:12:52,300
It seems to me you wouldn't raise the question

376
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:53,300
unless you had a lot of experience

377
00:12:53,300 --> 00:12:55,300
that life is not so good.

378
00:12:55,300 --> 00:12:58,300
I mean, in other words, it's a reaction to...

379
00:12:58,300 --> 00:12:59,300
What do you think that is?

380
00:12:59,300 --> 00:13:01,300
...having had so much experience

381
00:13:01,300 --> 00:13:04,300
of disappointment or suffering.

382
00:13:04,300 --> 00:13:09,300
Would you say that we are not conscious

383
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:13,300
of the whole movement of thought?

384
00:13:13,300 --> 00:13:15,300
No, but I mean, I think to most people

385
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:17,300
they would say that's only very natural.

386
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:19,300
I mean, I've had a lot of experience

387
00:13:19,300 --> 00:13:20,300
of suffering.

388
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:21,300
I mean, I've had a lot of experience

389
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:23,300
of suffering and disappointment and danger,

390
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:25,300
and that's unpleasant.

391
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:28,300
And I would like to be able to anticipate

392
00:13:28,300 --> 00:13:30,300
that everything is going to be good.

393
00:13:30,300 --> 00:13:31,300
Yes.

394
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:32,300
It would seem...

395
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:33,300
I mean, at first sight it would seem

396
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:36,300
that that's really quite natural.

397
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:38,300
But I mean, you're saying it's not now,

398
00:13:38,300 --> 00:13:39,300
that something is deeply wrong with it.

399
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:41,300
Yes, we are saying there is no such thing

400
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:45,300
as psychological security.

401
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:47,300
We have defined what we mean by security.

402
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:48,300
Yes.

403
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:49,300
We don't have to beat it over and over.

404
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:50,300
No, no, no.

405
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:52,300
Yes, but is it clear now that these hopes

406
00:13:52,300 --> 00:13:53,300
are really vain hopes?

407
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:55,300
I mean, that should be obvious.

408
00:13:55,300 --> 00:13:57,300
That I think is a good question.

409
00:13:57,300 --> 00:13:59,300
You mean, is it...

410
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:02,300
You see, Krishnaji, he's raising a good question.

411
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:03,300
It's this whole business you're saying.

412
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:07,300
Is it meaningful to look for security?

413
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:09,300
Is there such a thing?

414
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:11,300
Sir, there is death at the end of everything.

415
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:14,300
Yes.

416
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:17,300
You want to be secure for the next ten years,

417
00:14:17,300 --> 00:14:19,300
that's all, or fifty years.

418
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:22,300
Afterwards, it doesn't matter.

419
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:25,300
Or it does matter, then you believe in something.

420
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:28,300
That there is God, you'll sit next to God

421
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:32,300
on his right hand, or whatever it is you believe.

422
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:36,300
So I'm trying to find out

423
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:42,300
not only that there is no permanency psychologically,

424
00:14:42,300 --> 00:14:44,300
which means no tomorrow psychologically.

425
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:46,300
Yes, but that hasn't yet come out clearly.

426
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:48,300
Of course, of course, of course.

427
00:14:48,300 --> 00:14:51,300
You see, we can say empirically we know

428
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:53,300
that these hopes for security are false,

429
00:14:53,300 --> 00:14:55,300
because first of all, you say there is death.

430
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:58,300
Secondly, you can't count on anything.

431
00:14:58,300 --> 00:15:00,300
No matter materially, everything changes.

432
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:02,300
Everything is in flux.

433
00:15:02,300 --> 00:15:05,300
Mentally, everything in your head is changing all the time.

434
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:07,300
You can't count on your feelings,

435
00:15:07,300 --> 00:15:09,300
you can't count on enjoying a certain thing

436
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:11,300
that you enjoy now,

437
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:13,300
or you can't count on being healthy,

438
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:16,300
you can't count on the money.

439
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:17,300
And you can't rely on your wife,

440
00:15:17,300 --> 00:15:18,300
you can't rely on your husband,

441
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:19,300
you can't rely on nothing.

442
00:15:19,300 --> 00:15:20,300
Right, right.

443
00:15:20,300 --> 00:15:21,300
So that's a fact,

444
00:15:21,300 --> 00:15:24,300
but I'm saying you're suggesting something deeper.

445
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:25,300
Yes.

446
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:28,300
I mean, we don't base ourselves only on that absurd fact.

447
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:30,300
No, that's very superficial.

448
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:35,300
All right, yes, I'm with you there.

449
00:15:35,300 --> 00:15:40,300
So is there then, if there is no real security,

450
00:15:40,300 --> 00:15:47,300
basic, deep, then is there a tomorrow, psychologically?

451
00:15:48,300 --> 00:15:49,300
Yes.

452
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:55,300
And then you take away all hope.

453
00:15:55,300 --> 00:16:00,300
If there is no tomorrow, you take away all hope.

454
00:16:00,300 --> 00:16:02,300
Well, what you mean by tomorrow is the tomorrow

455
00:16:02,300 --> 00:16:04,300
in which things will get better, I mean.

456
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:10,300
Get better, with better, more, greater success,

457
00:16:10,300 --> 00:16:12,300
greater understanding, greater...

458
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:13,300
More love.

459
00:16:13,300 --> 00:16:16,300
More love, you know, the whole business.

460
00:16:18,300 --> 00:16:21,300
I think that's a little quick, that jump.

461
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:27,300
And I think that there's a jump there,

462
00:16:27,300 --> 00:16:31,300
because as I hear you, I hear you saying,

463
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:33,300
there is no security.

464
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:35,300
But it is so.

465
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:36,300
It is so.

466
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:40,300
But for me to say, or to really say,

467
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:43,300
look, I know there's no security.

468
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:45,300
Why don't you say that?

469
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:47,300
That's what I'm getting at.

470
00:16:47,300 --> 00:16:49,300
Why don't I say that?

471
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:50,300
Well, isn't it a fact that there's no...

472
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:51,300
Why do you think I don't?

473
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:52,300
I don't know.

474
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:53,300
Isn't it, first of all, a fact that,

475
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:55,300
just an observed fact that there isn't anything

476
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:57,300
you could count on, psychologically?

477
00:16:57,300 --> 00:17:00,300
Right, but you see, I think there's an action there

478
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:02,300
that Krishnaji is saying, well, why don't you?

479
00:17:02,300 --> 00:17:03,300
Why don't what?

480
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:04,300
Why don't you?

481
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:07,300
He says, why don't you say there's no security?

482
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:13,300
Why don't I?

483
00:17:13,300 --> 00:17:14,300
Can I...

484
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:15,300
May I...

485
00:17:17,300 --> 00:17:23,300
Do you rationalise what we are saying about security?

486
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:31,300
Say yes, as an idea, or actually so?

487
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:34,300
I actually say it so, but then I say,

488
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:36,300
well, I'll keep doing it, I'll keep doing it.

489
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:38,300
No, no, no, no.

490
00:17:38,300 --> 00:17:44,300
We are asking, do you, when you hear there is no security,

491
00:17:44,300 --> 00:17:47,300
is it an abstracted idea?

492
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:51,300
Or an actual fact, like that table,

493
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:56,300
like your hand there, or those flowers?

494
00:17:56,300 --> 00:17:59,300
I think it mostly becomes an idea.

495
00:17:59,300 --> 00:18:00,300
That's just it.

496
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:02,300
Then why should it become an idea?

497
00:18:02,300 --> 00:18:04,300
That, I think, is the question.

498
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:08,300
Why does it become an idea?

499
00:18:08,300 --> 00:18:11,300
Is it part of your training?

500
00:18:11,300 --> 00:18:13,300
Yes. Part of my conditioning.

501
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:17,300
Part of real objection to see things as they are.

502
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:19,300
Right.

503
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:20,300
That's right.

504
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:23,300
Because it moves.

505
00:18:23,300 --> 00:18:25,300
It feels like it moves then.

506
00:18:25,300 --> 00:18:27,300
Do you feel that?

507
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:31,300
Well, it seems if you see that there is no security,

508
00:18:31,300 --> 00:18:34,300
then the self...

509
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:36,300
Well, I mean, it seems that...

510
00:18:36,300 --> 00:18:39,300
See, first of all, let's try to put it that

511
00:18:39,300 --> 00:18:41,300
there is something which seems to be there

512
00:18:41,300 --> 00:18:42,300
which is trying to protect itself.

513
00:18:42,300 --> 00:18:45,300
Namely, let's say that it seems to be a fact

514
00:18:45,300 --> 00:18:47,300
that the self is there.

515
00:18:47,300 --> 00:18:49,300
If you see what I'm driving at.

516
00:18:49,300 --> 00:18:50,300
Of course.

517
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:53,300
And if the self is there, it requires security.

518
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:55,300
And therefore, this creates a resistance

519
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:57,300
to accepting that as a fact

520
00:18:57,300 --> 00:19:00,300
and puts it as an idea only.

521
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:01,300
You see what I mean?

522
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:07,300
It seems that the factuality of the self being there

523
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:09,300
has not been denied.

524
00:19:09,300 --> 00:19:12,300
The apparent factuality.

525
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:13,300
Right.

526
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:14,300
Right.

527
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:16,300
But why hasn't it been?

528
00:19:16,300 --> 00:19:19,300
Why do you think it hasn't been?

529
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:20,300
I mean, what happens...

530
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:24,300
Is it that you refuse to see things as they are?

531
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:29,300
Is it that one refuses to see that one is stupid?

532
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:30,300
Not you.

533
00:19:30,300 --> 00:19:32,300
I mean, one is stupid.

534
00:19:32,300 --> 00:19:33,300
Yes.

535
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:37,300
That to acknowledge that one is stupid is already...

536
00:19:37,300 --> 00:19:38,300
You follow?

537
00:19:38,300 --> 00:19:39,300
Yes.

538
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:40,300
Yes.

539
00:19:40,300 --> 00:19:41,300
I mean, it's like you say to me,

540
00:19:41,300 --> 00:19:43,300
you refuse to acknowledge you're stupid.

541
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:45,300
Let's say it's me.

542
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:46,300
What is...

543
00:19:46,300 --> 00:19:48,300
That means that I...

544
00:19:48,300 --> 00:19:51,300
Then I've got to do something, it feels like.

545
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:52,300
No.

546
00:19:52,300 --> 00:19:54,300
I mean, something happens to me.

547
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:56,300
Not yet.

548
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:59,300
Action comes through perception,

549
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:03,300
not through ideation.

550
00:20:03,300 --> 00:20:05,300
I'm glad you're getting into this.

551
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:07,300
Yes.

552
00:20:07,300 --> 00:20:10,300
Doesn't it seem that as long as there is the sense of self,

553
00:20:10,300 --> 00:20:14,300
the self must say that it is perfect, eternal, and so on?

554
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:15,300
Do you see it?

555
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:18,300
Of course, of course.

556
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:19,300
But what do you think it is?

557
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:22,300
What makes it so hard to say...

558
00:20:22,300 --> 00:20:23,300
Is this what you mean, by the way,

559
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:27,300
when you talk about the destruction in creation?

560
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:31,300
In other words, is there something here about the destruction that I'm not...

561
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:32,300
You must destroy that.

562
